    "create.CrushingWheelControllerBlockMixin",
    "create.DieselGeneratorBurnerTemperatureMixin",
    /*
     * Disabled 2026-10-01 - the fan overheat guard moved into the rebuilt
     * woodencog_wildfire mod itself:
     *
     *   create.FanOverheatMixin - relocated.
     *       It destroyed an item that a blasting fan had heated past its ceiling, both as a
     *       dropped entity and as an item carried on a belt. Every item a fan heats passes
     *       through Wooden Cog, so the guard belongs with the fan temperatures it protects.
     *       woodencog_wildfire injects it itself at the same priority of 900
     *       (net.chauvedev.woodencog.mixin.MixinFanOverheat, with the logic in
     *       net.chauvedev.woodencog.compat.create.FanOverheatGuard) and reads the two
     *       ceilings from woodencog-common.toml under [woodencog.fan] instead of from
     *       wildfires-fan-heat.toml. The class is kept in the source tree for the case that
     *       Wildfires has to run without woodencog_wildfire again.
     *       Keeping this entry as well would install a second head injection on both of the
     *       same methods, at the same priority, and one of the two would find the item already
     *       discarded.
     *
     * To re-enable it, move the entry back into the array below - but only after removing the
     * woodencog mixin named above and registering FanHeatConfig in Wildfires.java again.
     */
    // "create.FanOverheatMixin",
    "create.KineticBlockEntityMixin",
    "create.ProcessingRecipeMixin",
    "create.RecipeApplierHeatMixin",
    "createmetallurgy.CastingTableMoldHeatMixin",
    /*
     * Disabled 2026-09-30 - the three Wooden Cog patches either moved into the
     * rebuilt woodencog_wildfire mod itself or turned out not to be needed:
     *
     *   create.WoodenCogForgeHeatLevelMixin - obsolete.
     *       Wooden Cog commit 582c633 changed tempFromBlockstate's multiplier from
     *       Heat.maxVisibleTemperature() (1600) to the configured blaze_burner_seething,
     *       which this pack sets to 2300 and which is present in woodencog 1.2.17.
     *       Heat level 7 now reverse-computes to 2300C and level 8 to 2683C, so both
     *       already reach SEETHING. The 433.3C shortfall this mixin existed to fix is gone.
     *
     *   create.WoodenCogMoldHeatMixin - dead code.
     *       The last woodencog:filling mould recipe is commented out in
     *       kubejs/server_scripts/thirace/recipes/glass_mold.js and pouring moved to
     *       createmetallurgy:casting_in_table, so AdvancedRecipe.onResultStackSingle is no
     *       longer on any live path. CastingTableMoldHeatMixin, still enabled above,
     *       covers the route that is actually used.
     *
     *   create.WoodenCogMoreBurnerTemperatureMixin - ported natively.
     *       Its heat-level mapping and gradual warm-up now live in
     *       net.chauvedev.woodencog.compat.createmoreburners.CMBIntegrationImpl
     *       inside woodencog_wildfire, so keeping this would only duplicate the same
     *       mapping from the outside.
     *
     * To re-enable one, move its entry back into the array below.
     */
    // "create.WoodenCogForgeHeatLevelMixin",
    // "create.WoodenCogMoldHeatMixin",
    // "create.WoodenCogMoreBurnerTemperatureMixin",
    "farmersdelight.BasketBlockEntityMixin",
